Class: Blueprint (A plan to make other objects)

Object: Has attribute to perform tasks (Object of real-life application)

Instance: An object maintaining its copy of an attribute (Individual object)

Access Modifier (including public and private): Allows certain access to methods, classes, and objects (+ → Public; - → Private; # → Protected)

Instance Variable (Field): Variables within classes (One particular property of a class)

Constructor Method: Initializes objects of a class when created. To build an object.

Unified Modeling Language Class Diagram: Visualizes and models a system with classes

Import Statement: Import methods from other classes (import package.class.method)

Parameter: Placeholder of method

Argument: Values shared with the parameters

Set Method: Modifier methods (modify instance variables)

Get Method: Access methods (return the instance variable)

Primitive Type: Stores one value at its declared time (boolean, char, int, long, double, float, short)

Reference Type: Refers to an object in a program (String). Stores the location of the object in the computer’s memory. Default is null
